The whole corpus is what t/run.sh scores against; it fetches the tarball into
.scratch/ on first run and caches it there. This subset exists so that
`make test` still means something with no network: it is chosen for coverage
rather than for size -- every colour type, every bit depth, both interlace
modes, all five filters, tRNS in all three forms, the 1-byte IDAT split, two
zlib levels, four matched interlaced/non-interlaced pairs, and all 14 of the
deliberately corrupt x*.png files, which are the ones that must be rejected.
